fit-axis-skipped = Axis { $arg }: not fitted. The trace has to move it in both directions.
fit-mass = Moved mass, axis { $arg }. Add this to the masses that move with the axis. The trace cannot tell load mass from rotor and pulley inertia.
fit-viscous = Viscous friction, axis { $arg }. Scale the viscous friction of the axis's guide and of the motor shafts by this factor; the trace cannot tell the two apart.
fit-coulomb = Coulomb friction, axis { $arg }. Scale the Coulomb friction and stiction of the axis's guide and of the motor shafts by this factor; the trace cannot tell the two apart.
fit-constant = Constant force, axis { $arg }. The measured axis needs this much more than the config gives: a weight, an incline or a cable pull the config lacks.
fit-stiffness = Stiffness between motor and load: { $arg }. Scale the belt stiffness by this factor. It holds only once the masses are right, so correct those first and sweep again.
fit-no-resonance = No stiffness fitted: the measured sweep or the config's own shows no dip with both flanks inside the swept range.
fit-joints-skipped = Not fitted in the motors' coordinates: the trace has to turn every motor in both directions.
fit-payload = Payload: { $arg }. Scale the payload's mass by this factor.
fit-joint-inertia = Inertia at motor { $arg }. Add this to what the motor turns: its rotor, or the arm or link on its joint, reflected to the motor; the trace cannot tell the two apart.
fit-joint-viscous = Viscous friction at motor { $arg }. Add this, at the motor shaft, to the viscous friction of the motor and its joint.
fit-joint-coulomb = Coulomb friction at motor { $arg }. Add this, at the motor shaft, to the Coulomb friction of the motor and its joint; the trace cannot tell it from gearbox losses.
fit-joint-constant = Constant torque at motor { $arg }. The measured motor needs this much more than the config gives: a weight, a spring or a cable pull the config lacks.
fit-alike = Not told apart by this trace: { $arg }. Only their sum is known; a trace that swings every axis over more of its range at several frequencies separates them.
fit-payload-step = Payload picked or dropped during the trace, at { $arg } (factor on its mass before → after). Fit the rest of the trace with these two; the config holds one payload.
fit-link-mass = Link { $arg }. Scale the link's mass and inertia in the URDF by this factor.
fit-link-moment = First moment along { $arg }. Add this to the link's mass times its centre of mass along that axis of its frame, in the URDF.
fit-combined = Not told apart: { $arg }. The change shown for the first stands for its own change plus each factor times the other's. Where the rigid model only knows their sum no trace separates them; otherwise a trace that moves the joints they act through over more of their range may.
fit-no-effect = No effect on the motor torques, so not fitted: { $arg }.
fit-move-not-excited = No stiffness from this trace: its moves do not ring the load on its springs enough against the noise (the best factor { $arg }; a standard error above a tenth of the factor, or the factor at an end of 0.25 to 4, is refused). Moves with steeper acceleration ramps, at higher speed, or a sweep do.
fit-move-stiffness = Stiffness between motor and load, from the moves: { $arg }. Scale the stiffness the fit replayed (the belts' unless --stiffness-key named another) by this factor. It holds only once the masses are right, so correct those first and fit again.
fit-move-no-key = No stiffness from this trace: the config has no number at { $arg }. Name the spring between motor and load with --stiffness-key.
path-deviation = The planned path is off the given lines and arcs by up to { $arg } mm (transition curves, and arcs that end beside their stated end).
